@page "/recipes/turkey-picnic-sandwich"

<PageTitle>Turkey Picnic Sandwich</PageTitle>

<div class="recipe-detail-page">
    <section class="recipe-hero">
        <div class="recipe-copy">
            <h1>Turkey Picnic Sandwich</h1>

            <p>
                A sturdy, artisan-style pressed sub layered with lean roasted turkey, 
                creamy provolone, mashed lemon avocado, and crisp greens.
            </p>

            <div class="meta-row">
                <span class="meta-pill">
                    <span class="meta-icon">◔</span>
                    <span>Prep: 20 min</span>
                </span>
                <span class="meta-pill">
                    <span class="meta-icon">◔</span>
                    <span>Cook: 0 min</span>
                </span>
                <span class="meta-pill">
                    <span class="meta-icon">◔</span>
                    <span>Serves: 4</span>
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="recipe-hero-image">
            <img src="images/turkey-picnic-sandwich.jpg" alt="Honey fried chicken" />
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="scallop-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <section class="recipe-grid">
        <article class="info-card ingredients-card">
            <h2>
                <span class="list-mark"></span>
                Ingredients List
            </h2>

            <div class="ingredient-group">
                <ul>
                    <li>1 large ciabatta loaf or crusty baguette</li>
                    <li>250g sliced deli turkey breast</li>
                    <li>6 slices provolone cheese</li>
                    <li>1 ripe avocado, mashed with 1 teaspoon lemon juice, salt, and pepper</li>
                    <li>2 tablespoons mayonnaise mixed with 1 tablespoon Dijon mustard</li>
                    <li>1 cup dry baby arugula or alfalfa sprouts</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
            <h2>
                <span class="list-mark"></span>
                Step-by-Step Guide
            </h2>

            <ol>
                <li>Lay your ciabatta or baguette flat on a cutting board and use a long serrated bread knife to slice it completely in half horizontally, keeping your blade perfectly level.</li>
                <li>Use a spatula to spread the mustard-mayonnaise mixture evenly across the cut side of the top bread half, and spread your freshly seasoned, lemon-infused mashed avocado across the cut side of the bottom half.</li>
                <li>Lay your slices of provolone cheese flat across both halves of the bread, making sure the cheese completely covers the spreads; this fat barrier prevents the bread from absorbing moisture and becoming mushy over time.</li>
                <li>Pile your sliced deli turkey breast generously over the cheese on the bottom half, then top with your fresh arugula or alfalfa sprouts—ensuring the greens have been thoroughly spun or patted dry with paper towels beforehand.</li>
                <li>Close the sandwich with the top bread layer, wrap the entire loaf tightly in parchment paper or aluminum foil like a package, and place a heavy object like a cast-iron skillet or weighted cutting board directly on top of it inside the refrigerator for 30 minutes.</li>
                <li>Keep the sandwich wrapped up tight and use your serrated knife to slice through both the paper and bread into individual servings; this keeps the layers perfectly compressed and structurally sound until you unzip your picnic basket.</li>
            </ol>
        </article>
    </section>
</div>
